# 🔟 Meeting Time

Two people are 300 km apart.

They move toward each other at:

$$
40\ km/h
$$

and:

$$
60\ km/h
$$

Relative speed:

$$
40+60=100
$$

Time:

$$
\frac{300}{100}
$$

$$
\boxed{3\ hours}
$$

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Average Speed 🚨

Never automatically do:

$$
\frac{S_1+S_2}{2}
$$

Average speed is:

$$
\boxed{
\frac{Total\ Distance}{Total\ Time}
}
$$

---

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Equal Distance

If equal distances are travelled at speeds \(a\) and \(b\):

$$
\boxed{
Average\ Speed=\frac{2ab}{a+b}
}
$$

Example:

Equal distances at:

$$
40,\ 60\ km/h
$$

$$
Average=
\frac{2(40)(60)}{40+60}
$$

$$
=\frac{4800}{100}
$$

$$
\boxed{48\ km/h}
$$

---

# 1️⃣3️⃣ Equal Time

If equal amounts of time are spent at speeds \(a\) and \(b\):

$$
\boxed{
Average=\frac{a+b}{2}
}
$$

Example:

$$
40,\ 60
$$

$$
\boxed{50\ km/h}
$$

### 🧠 Remember:

> **Equal distance → harmonic mean**

> **Equal time → arithmetic mean**

