# 1️⃣4️⃣ Trains 🚆

Train questions use:

$$
\boxed{Time=\frac{Distance}{Speed}}
$$

But the important part is determining the **effective distance**.

---

# 1️⃣5️⃣ Train Crossing a Pole

Suppose:

Train length:

$$
200m
$$

Speed:

$$
20m/s
$$

A pole has negligible length.

Distance travelled by train:

$$
200m
$$

Therefore:

$$
Time=\frac{200}{20}
$$

$$
\boxed{10s}
$$

---

# 1️⃣6️⃣ Train Crossing a Platform

Train length:

$$
200m
$$

Platform:

$$
300m
$$

Total distance:

$$
200+300
$$

$$
=500m
$$

At:

$$
25m/s
$$

Time:

$$
500/25
$$

$$
\boxed{20s}
$$

🔥 Memory:

> **Pole → Train length**

> **Platform → Train + Platform length**

---

# 1️⃣7️⃣ Two Trains Crossing

Train A:

$$
100m
$$

Train B:

$$
150m
$$

Opposite directions.

Effective distance:

$$
100+150=250m
$$

If speeds are:

$$
20m/s,\ 30m/s
$$

Relative speed:

$$
20+30=50m/s
$$

Time:

$$
250/50
$$

$$
\boxed{5s}
$$

---

# 1️⃣8️⃣ Two Trains Same Direction

Train A:

$$
150m
$$

Train B:

$$
100m
$$

Speeds:

$$
50m/s,\ 30m/s
$$

Relative speed:

$$
50-30=20m/s
$$

Effective distance:

$$
150+100=250m
$$

Time:

$$
250/20
$$

$$
\boxed{12.5s}
$$

