# 🧮 2️⃣5️⃣ GATE-Style Example

A person travels half the distance at 30 km/h and the remaining half at 60 km/h.

Since distances are equal:

$$
Average=\frac{2(30)(60)}{30+60}
$$

$$
=\frac{3600}{90}
$$

$$
\boxed{40km/h}
$$

---

# 🧮 2️⃣6️⃣ Another Example

A car travels for 2 hours at 40 km/h and 3 hours at 60 km/h.

Distance 1:

$$
2\times40=80
$$

Distance 2:

$$
3\times60=180
$$

Total distance:

$$
260
$$

Total time:

$$
5
$$

Average:

$$
260/5
$$

$$
\boxed{52km/h}
$$

