# 🗣️ Communication Practice — 100–200 Words

### Topic: **How I Handle Difficult Problems**

When I face a difficult problem, I try not to become overwhelmed by the entire problem at once. First, I identify exactly what is being asked and separate the problem into smaller parts. Then I look for the information that is given and determine what is missing. I usually start with a simple approach because it helps me understand the underlying logic. After that, I look for ways to improve the solution in terms of time, memory, or accuracy. I also test my reasoning with small examples before considering the problem solved. If I make a mistake, I try to understand why it happened instead of simply memorizing the correct answer. This approach is useful not only for aptitude questions and programming problems but also for real software engineering tasks. I believe consistent practice makes difficult problems more manageable and gradually improves both confidence and problem-solving ability.

